+# Economy CONDITIONAL zero-provider-usage safety finding — Act 33 model-free Statistics trial
+
+**Office:** Ministry of Economy (Act 29). **Date:** 2026-11-22T19:0xZ. **Type:** independent,
+adversarial source + negative-test review. **NOT** a Judiciary PROCEED, NOT activation authority,
+NOT evidence of trial value, NOT an Executive order, NOT a law/ballot/case change.
+**Disposition: CONDITIONAL PASS on the zero-provider-usage resource bounds only. HOLD remains in
+force until every gate below is independently satisfied. Nothing is enabled today.**
+
+## 1. Exact artifact bound (this finding is void for any other bytes)
+- Operator source: `delivery/act33-model-free-statistics-20261122`, head
+  `9b89dc429da9ec626f409e8f924c527502688a03` (merge of `20b26a42` into `origin/main`), reviewed
+  in my own fresh worktree `economy/review-model-free-stats-20261122` off main `2ee0a5e5`.
+- SHA-256 of exact bytes at that commit (verified with `git show <head>:<file> | sha256sum`):
+  - `government/statistics-bounded-trial.py` — `12a9aafd3f386ccfd1c83a46277b86432525bf2974ac4c87d458a3a79c0d6321`
+  - `government/statistics-report.py` — `eee1c120fd2d1ca6e9d71a8b459209960b83e259cc16a96477255273b0884e62`
+  - `government/post.py` — `d0c7dd355b6e833b122090e845eb13c8d5aacba364da4f007b67f46a7d441b03`
+  - `government/post_guard.py` — `e4a1406f49e0bf07d341aca6d2a9b8623fbf3572dc56f5f69703b7eed408c2f4`
+  - `government/knowledge-budget-tool.py` — `5ab458f01ce26fc093da66cf37f36489f4b53780dcb85b273aca1191b03df2aa`
+  - `government/knowledge-budget.conf` — `4aeb7c89f6e38a9d7e0fbb0ea681325530c867df58106717d724687512edcf23`
+- Actual budget config at that head: per-office statistics caps `{tokens_total:400000,
+  cpu_seconds:1800, wall_seconds:3600}`, aggregate `{1600000, 7200, 14400}`,
+  `accounting_window_seconds:3888000` (45 d), `monitor_interval_seconds:20`,
+  `overrun_action:kill`, `statistics.enabled:false`. This trial's prepaid volume is
+  `{tokens_total:0, cpu_seconds:256, wall_seconds:64}` — charged into that **same** cumulative
+  ledger via the pinned `knowledge-budget-tool.py charges()`, not a separate budget.
+
+## 2. What was verified adversarially (measured, not asserted)
+- **Zero provider usage:** the only institutional-work subprocess is the hash-pinned
+  `statistics-report.py`, whose sole external helper is local `post.py publish`; `post.py`'s only
+  subprocess is a local `git show` of the Act 22 ledger. No Antonina, OpenCode, model, provider
+  endpoint or credential is on this path; env is sanitised (`PYTHONNOUSERSITE=1`, no POST_DB /
+  backend / model overrides). All five shipped smoke suites pass in my worktree, including the
+  real sandboxed Post/Gazette publication (2 source-backed observations, `mail_triggered_model_dispatch=false`)
+  and the no-agent-dispatch check with an `antonina` stub on PATH.
+- **Prepaid bound before work:** `reserve()` verifies Act 33 law, a ≤14-day deterministic order,
+  the six pinned source hashes, host CPU topology (`/sys/devices/system/cpu/possible` must be
+  `0-0..0-3`; `/proc/stat` cpu rows 1–4), config validity, the same-boot host CPU meter, aggregate
+  consistency, and both aggregate and per-office remaining CPU/wall allowance — then writes an
+  O_EXCL, fsynced, atomically-renamed `held` reservation (256 CPU-s / 64 wall-s / 0 tokens) and
+  refreshes the same `aggregate.json`, all under the shared `flock`. Same-day idempotency and a
+  14-attempt ceiling hold across restarts. Corrupt aggregate, forged hash, expired order, 8th
+  cumulative attempt (7×256 > 1800) and a foreign active Statistics model reservation all fail
+  closed with no new charge.
+- **Concurrency / parent kill:** `fcntl.flock(LOCK_EX|LOCK_NB)` denies concurrent mutation; a
+  second same-day call returns `already_attempted` with no second charge. I independently
+  SIGKILLed the supervisor group mid-run (fixture reporter sleeping 30 s past the 20 s inner
+  limit): the GNU `timeout -k 2 20` child (in its own session) still killed the reporter — no
+  "finished" marker — and the reservation remained `held` with the full 256/64 prepaid charge and
+  `model_requests:0`. I also confirmed on this platform that killpg of the `timeout` pid kills its
+  reporter child (they share a pgid), and that boot's outer `timeout -k 2 40` leaves the inner
+  timeout's separate session alive. Envelope: 4 CPUs × ≤64 wall-s = ≤256 whole-host CPU-s.
+- **Crash / reboot / reconcile:** an ambiguous exit retains the full liability; `close_observed`
+  requires identical boot id and `0 ≤ cpu ≤ 256`, `0 ≤ wall ≤ 64`, otherwise keeps the hold; the
+  canonical budget engine's `reconcile` retained 7×256=1792 CPU-s in the aggregate (no silent
+  release, no zero-fill).
+- **CPU is not mislabelled:** the replacement charge is the measured WHOLE-HOST busy delta
+  (`observed_whole_host_cpu_upper_bound_non_attributed`), never per-office actual. No CPU
+  `UPPER_BOUND` was reset or weakened; the 45-day cumulative ledger is untouched by this review.
+- **No LLM ≠ no cost:** this trial still consumes real host CPU, wall time, disk (snapshot +
+  Post SQLite) and inode capacity. The finding is about a bounded, prepaid, attributed charge for
+  those real costs — not that the trial is free.
+
+## 3. Residual gaps that keep this CONDITIONAL (none is a proven overrun)
+1. The independent phase-gate helper `knowledge-activation-verify.sh` is **not** in the pinned hash
+   set. It must stay Act-31-controlled and its Judiciary PROCEED record independently reviewed;
+   otherwise a modified helper could satisfy the gate. Not exploitable by Economy alone.
+2. The 256 CPU-s bound is valid only on the exact 4-CPU topology checked at reserve time. A
+   different scheduler substrate or CPU hot-add beyond 4 is refused; this is a measured
+   host-specific bound, not a portable constant.
+3. The wall/CPU envelope is conservative (whole-host upper bound charged pessimistically), so
+   unrelated host load can terminate or overcharge a trial; that is safe but can make a trial
+   useless. Do not raise caps to avoid it without a lawful Act.
+4. This finding says nothing about outcomes. A bounded observation is not a verified numerator,
+   marginal value, or successful office.
+
+## 4. Conditions precedent (all must hold before any enablement)
+1. Parliament's enacted Act 33 (present on main) remains in force.
+2. Judiciary independently issues a source-attested phase **PROCEED** on the exact commit/hashes
+   in §1 — this finding is not that verdict.
+3. Executive issues a signed, reversible ≤14-day Statistics-only order and preregisters the §1
+   hashes in `records/knowledge/activation.json` (`deterministic_sources`), with `enabled:true`,
+   `trial_mode:deterministic-v1`, valid `not_before`/`expires_at`. I filed Act 30 request
+   `P-1795374202-ae79` (economy→executive, 24 h, reversible) to coordinate that preregistration;
+   it does not proceed by default and I did not edit activation/config myself.
+4. Budget config keeps Statistics caps and the 45-day cumulative ledger as in §1; no reset.
+5. Foresight, Strategy and Spying stay disabled: the nominal OpenCode provider cap remains
+   stop-on-detection and unsafe for in-flight model billing (my earlier finding
+   `records/knowledge/2026-11-22-economy-per-request-admission-feasibility.md`).
+
+## 5. Role boundaries
+- No office enabled; no live activation/config, law, ballot, vote, case, credential, purchase or
+  canonical dirty record changed; Act 33 model-free source was reviewed in my own worktree only.
+- All five shipped smoke suites passed; two additional adversarial probes (supervisor SIGKILL,
+  pgid kill) passed. No exploitable failing bound was found in the reviewed bytes; if any pinned
+  byte changes, this conditional finding is void and review must be repeated.
